From: Thorch contributors
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: qcs8550-ayn-thor: reserve ramoops memory

Give the Thor a persistent crash store. The shared AYN reserved-memory
node is unlabeled, so extend it by path instead of declaring a second
root-level "reserved-memory" node: a duplicate node name is a dtc error
and would fail the DTB build. The region is allocated by early memblock
from the top of RAM rather than pinned to a guessed address, like the
stock Thor device tree does, and is marked no-map so the kernel keeps it
out of the linear map and the allocator.

The record/console/ftrace/pmsg budgets leave room for one oops record,
the last kmsg, a persistent function trace and one pmsg record inside a
4 MiB window. CONFIG_PSTORE_RAM now binds against the node via the
size-based reserved-memory fallback.

Whether the bootloader preserves this RAM across a hard reset on this
board must be validated on the device before relying on it.

Ported from linux-thorch 5029454f ("feat: add Thor persistent crash
storage and opt-in sync diagnostics") and 346d69ca ("fix: resolve
dynamically reserved ramoops memory"). The original declared a new
root-level reserved-memory node, which collides with the node that
qcs8550-ayn-common.dtsi already defines; this version extends that node
by path.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs8550-ayn-thor.dts | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
  1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs8550-ayn-thor.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs8550-ayn-thor.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs8550-ayn-thor.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs8550-ayn-thor.dts
@@ -6,7 +6,28 @@
 /dts-v1/;
 
 #include "qcs8550-ayn-common.dtsi"
 
+/*
+ * The shared AYN reserved-memory node has no label, so extend it by
+ * path. Like the stock Thor DT, allocate instead of guessing a DRAM
+ * address; early memblock allocation excludes firmware regions.
+ * Cross-reset retention must be validated on this bootloader.
+ */
+&{/reserved-memory} {
+	ramoops {
+		compatible = "ramoops";
+		no-map;
+		size = <0 0x400000>;
+		alignment = <0 0x400000>;
+		alloc-ranges = <0 0 0xffffffff 0xffffffff>;
+		record-size = <0x40000>;
+		console-size = <0x100000>;
+		ftrace-size = <0x100000>;
+		pmsg-size = <0x40000>;
+		mem-type = <0>;
+	};
+};
+
 / {
 	model = "AYN Thor";
 	compatible = "ayn,thor", "qcom,qcs8550", "qcom,sm8550";
